  description: Potassium is a chemical element with symbol K (derived from Neo-Latin,
    kalium) and atomic number 19. It was first isolated from potash, the ashes of
    plants, from which its name is derived. In the Periodic table, potassium is one
    of seven elements in column (group) 1 (alkali metals):they all have a single
    valence electron in their outer electron shell, which they readily give up to
    create an atom with a positive charge - a cation, and combine with anions to
    form salts.
